==Italian==

===Verb form===
'''conduco'''

# ''first-person singular indicative present of [[condurre]]''

[[Category:Italian verb forms]]

----

==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{term|con|lang=la}} + {{term|duco|dūcō|lead|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/konˈduː.koː/|lang=la}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|conduco|condūcō|conducere|condūcere|conduxi|condūxī|conductum|conductum}}

# {{transitive|lang=la}} I [[lead]], [[bring]] or [[draw]] together; [[assemble]], [[collect]].
# {{transitive|lang=la}} I [[connect]], [[join]], [[unite]]; [[close up]]; [[coagulate]].
# {{transitive|lang=la}} I [[hire]], [[rent]], [[employ]], take on [[lease]], [[undertake]]; [[farm]]; [[bribe]].
# {{intransitive|lang=la}} I am [[conducive]] to, [[contribute]] to something by being [[useful]], I am of use or [[profitable]], [[serve]].

